  "notes": "Entirely business-type entity; governmental fields null. Amounts in thousands as printed ('Dollars in thousands'), units 1000. Trimmed PDF: p1 MD&A text (overview of statements, no figures), p2 Balance Sheet, p3 Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position, p4 Statement of Cash Flows, p5 cash flows continued (reconciliation of operating income, no new totals), p6 notes text; no detail schedules. Receipts = total operating revenues 350,029 + interest income 10,490 + other income 577; disbursements = total operating expenses 270,015 + interest expense, payment in lieu of taxes, City Dividend. Net 48,408 = printed change in net position; 523,194 + 48,408 = 571,602. Capital contributions 1,948 and Plant costs recovered through capital contributions (1,948) are netted in business_type.other_financing (0, computed), as in FY2025. No single printed receipts/disbursements totals; added up as noted. Balance sheet: total assets derived because the printed total combines assets and deferred outflows; the line printed 'Total deferred inflows of resources 759,445' is actually total liabilities 717,686 + deferred inflows 41,759 (label as printed is misleading; figures tie). Cash flow statement column header prints '2022' but the title says year ended December 31, 2023 and its ending cash 35,019 reconciles to the 2023 balance sheet (148,929 + 22,917 + 26,005 - 162,832 investments), so it was used as 2023. 'Reductions of future billings' deferred inflow has no matching category (left uncategorized). Read pages 1-6 of 6"
}
